---
import Lab from '../components/Lab';
import '../styles.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Saran Vashisht — A working case for ZeroGrunt</title>
    <meta name="description" content="An independent application for ZeroGrunt, built around a small invoice exception workflow." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://zerogrunt.saran.info/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Saran Vashisht — A working case for ZeroGrunt" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://zerogrunt.saran.info/" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="An invoice workflow you can put to the test." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://zerogrunt.saran.info/social.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Saran Vashisht: an invoice workflow you can put to the test" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="#top">SV <span>/</span> ZeroGrunt</a><span class="top-label">Independent application by Saran Vashisht</span><button id="present" class="text-button" type="button">Presentation mode <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></header>
    <main id="main">
      <p class="mobile-ownership">Independent application by Saran Vashisht</p>
      <section class="hero slide" id="top" data-title="Opening">
        <div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow light">A working case for ZeroGrunt <span>01 / 07</span></p><h1>An invoice workflow you can put to the test<span class="lime">.</span></h1><p class="hero-copy">Saurav, I wanted to try the problem in your post. I chose one invoice and built a small way to explore changing context, a lost response, a correction and its evaluation.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#lab">Try the invoice workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="under-link" href="#evidence">Explore the evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div><div class="hero-aside" aria-hidden="true"><div class="document-mark"><span>INVOICE</span><strong>000184</strong><div class="rule"></div><div class="mark-line"></div><div class="mark-line short"></div><div class="mark-total">INR 1,250.00 <span>↗</span></div></div><p>Printer maintenance<br />NORTHSTAR-IN<br /><strong>A fictional invoice for this exercise.</strong></p></div></div>
      </section>
      <section class="section slide" id="lab" data-title="Invoice lab"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / The invoice lab</p><h2>A printer maintenance invoice, from review to receipt.</h2></div><p>I picked a familiar expense because the interesting part is what happens when the coding, approver or posting outcome is uncertain. Choose a question to try it.</p></div><Lab client:load /></div></section>
      <section class="section pale slide" id="decisions" data-title="Engineering decisions"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Engineering decisions</p><h2>Four choices behind the demo.</h2><div class="decision-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Record which policy was used.</h3><p>Policy, entity and vendor records are authority; retrieved explanations are context. A changed policy can make an earlier approval stale.</p><a href="/?scenario=context#lab">Try changing the policy ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/zerogrunt-saran-info/blob/codex/zerogrunt-application/lab/core.mjs">Context code ↗</a></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Check the receipt after a timeout.</h3><p>Keep the business identity stable. After a lost response, inspect the receipt before deciding what happened.</p><a href="/?scenario=recovery#lab">Explore recovery ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/zerogrunt-saran-info/blob/codex/zerogrunt-application/lab/relay.mjs">Relay code ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/zerogrunt-saran-info/blob/codex/zerogrunt-application/lab/store.mjs">Store code ↗</a></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Separate a correction from a future rule.</h3><p>Start with a one-off fix. A scoped candidate needs a separate testing decision and human activation.</p><a href="/?scenario=correction#lab">Review a correction ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/zerogrunt-saran-info/blob/codex/zerogrunt-application/lab/core.mjs">Rule code ↗</a></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Compare the candidate with the baseline.</h3><p>Keep rejected cases and scope exclusions visible. A passing control is not evidence that a different candidate improved.</p><a href="/?scenario=evaluation#lab">Inspect evaluation ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/zerogrunt-saran-info/blob/codex/zerogrunt-application/lab/evaluate.mjs">Evaluation code ↗</a></div></article></div></div></section>
      <section class="section slide" id="work" data-title="Selected work"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Selected work</p><div class="section-heading"><h2>Where this way<br />of thinking comes from.</h2><p>Three projects, chosen for the problems they helped me understand.</p></div><div class="stories"><article><div class="story-number">01 <span>Integration & recovery</span></div><h3>Field Relay</h3><p>I built a browser reconciliation desk and a separate synthetic HTTP integration lab. The lab treats approved inputs, business identity and receipt readback as distinct concerns.</p><p class="scope">The browser and HTTP lab are separate. Neither is a live customer ERP integration.</p><a href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/field-relay/blob/main/docs/integration/CONTRACT.md">Read the contract ↗</a></article><article><div class="story-number">02 <span>Operational understanding</span></div><h3>Tetr Compass</h3><p>I built a portal around post-deposit documents, next tasks and staff follow-up. A student submitting a document and staff verifying it are different events.</p><p class="scope">The later fictional RAG guide is separate from the historical portal.</p><a href="https://saran.info/work/tetr-compass/">See the project ↗</a></article><article><div class="story-number">03 <span>Evaluation & judgment</span></div><h3>Listening Party</h3><p>Stricter retrieval candidates rejected useful requests, so I kept BM25 rather than treating a new approach as an automatic improvement.</p><p class="scope">A small synthetic comparison: 40 development and 34 held-out cases. It does not prove customer benefit.</p><a href="https://saran.info/work/listening-party/">See the project ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
      <section class="section dark slide" id="approach" data-title="How I build"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow light">04 / How I build with AI</p><h2>How this was built.</h2></div><div><p class="large-copy">I set the brief and used Codex to build and test this exercise. The code and recorded results are here to inspect; I’m learning to explain the choices and their limits.</p><p>My background is in enterprise support and automation, product and operations. Those experiences have made me pay attention to the person who has to resolve an exception when a process stops.</p></div></div></section>
      <section class="section slide" id="first-month" data-title="First month"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / A proposed first month</p><h2>Start close<br />to the work.</h2><p class="muted">A proposal, conditional on customer access and context, not an agreed roadmap.</p></div><ol class="timeline"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Observe</h3><p>Follow one finance workflow with the people doing the work. Find the real exceptions and handoffs.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Define</h3><p>Agree on states, source authority and what a person must review before an action.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Build & challenge</h3><p>Deliver one reviewed path, inject failures and evaluate proposed corrections against examples.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3>Learn in a bounded pilot</h3><p>Choose metrics with the operator, inspect misses and use the results to decide what comes next.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
      <section class="section finish slide" id="evidence" data-title="Contact and sources"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow light">06 / Continue the conversation</p><h2>Thanks for taking<br />a closer look<span class="lime">.</span></h2><p class="large-copy">I’d love to discuss the workflow, the tradeoffs, and what I would change with access to a real operator.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://saran.info/#contact">Contact Saran <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="under-link" href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/zerogrunt-saran-info">Inspect this project ↗</a></div><div class="footer-line"><span>Saran Vashisht · Independent application</span><span>Built with AI assistance · Synthetic data</span></div></div></section>
    </main>
    <nav id="presentation-controls" class="presentation-controls" aria-label="Presentation controls" hidden><button type="button" id="previous">← Previous</button><span id="progress" aria-live="polite"></span><button type="button" id="next">Next →</button><button type="button" id="exit">Exit presentation</button></nav>
    <script>
      const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#present');
      const controls = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#presentation-controls');
      const slides = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide'));
      const progress = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#progress');
      let current = 0;
      let active = false;
      function go(index: number) { current = Math.max(0, Math.min(slides.length - 1, index)); slides[current].scrollIntoView({behavior: matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 'instant' : 'smooth', block: 'start'}); if (progress) progress.textContent = `${current + 1} / ${slides.length} · ${slides[current].dataset.title}`; }
      function close() { active = false; if (controls) controls.hidden = true; button?.focus(); }
      button?.addEventListener('click', () => { active = true; if (controls) controls.hidden = false; const nearest = slides.reduce((best, slide, index) => Math.abs(slide.getBoundingClientRect().top) < Math.abs(slides[best].getBoundingClientRect().top) ? index : best, 0); go(nearest); });
      document.querySelector('#previous')?.addEventListener('click', () => go(current - 1));
      document.querySelector('#next')?.addEventListener('click', () => go(current + 1));
      document.querySelector('#exit')?.addEventListener('click', close);
      document.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => { if (!active) return; if (event.key === 'Escape') close(); if (event.target instanceof HTMLElement && /INPUT|SELECT|TEXTAREA/.test(event.target.tagName)) return; if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') { event.preventDefault(); go(current + 1); } if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') { event.preventDefault(); go(current - 1); } });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
